message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
title: "TRIGRS-PyWrap: Python wrapper for the TRIGRS landslide hazard model"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gómez"
    given-names: "Federico"
    email: "fjgomezc@eafit.edu.co"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8525-4354"
    affiliation: "SIATA, Sistema de Alerta Temprana de Antioquia; Universidad EAFIT"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-06-01"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/federicogmz/trigrs-pywrap"
url: "https://github.com/federicogmz/trigrs-pywrap"
abstract: >-
  Python wrapper for TRIGRS (Transient Rainfall Infiltration and Grid-Based
  Regional Slope-Stability). It automates DEM preprocessing, geological data
  rasterization, slope and flow-direction analysis, soil thickness estimation
  from the Catani et al. model, and batch parameter sensitivity runs, turning a
  closed, platform-specific reference implementation into scriptable geospatial
  workflows.
keywords:
  - "landslides"
  - "TRIGRS"
  - "slope stability"
  - "hazard assessment"
  - "rainfall infiltration"
  - "geohazards"
  - "geospatial"
  - "DEM"
